# Collaboration (Bandesca)

Follow **`AGENTS.md`** at the repo root for full wording. Summary:

- **Explain when it helps** — Short diagnosis and options before large patches, especially for “why” / “how to fix” questions.
- **Honor explicit limits** — “Review only” or “don’t write code” means no repo edits unless the user clearly wants implementation.
- **Small, reviewable diffs** — Scoped changes only; no drive-by refactors or filler. Match existing style and naming.
- **No slop** — Avoid unnecessary comments, abstractions, or extra docs the user didn’t ask for.
- **Verify in the real environment** — Run commands and use actual errors when possible instead of guessing.

Default posture: **guide like a careful teammate**, then implement in **minimal steps** the human can review and own.
